WEBVTT

00:26:00.140 --> 00:26:02.521
Since they couldn't erase
those demands altogether,

00:26:02.545 --> 00:26:05.165
Adrienne and her colleagues
turned to the next component

00:26:05.189 --> 00:26:07.027
of the demand, control, support model.

00:26:07.051 --> 00:26:09.016
And they did it in an unexpected way,

00:26:09.040 --> 00:26:11.106
which succeeded in reducing burnout.

00:26:11.130 --> 00:26:14.396
AB: We had taken
40,000 caregivers offline,

00:26:14.420 --> 00:26:16.276
trained them in empathy.

00:26:16.300 --> 00:26:18.176
AG: I'm ready to be wrong on this one,

00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:19.506
but it's surprising to me.

00:26:19.530 --> 00:26:22.776
I don't think I would have
ever wanted to train empathy

00:26:22.800 --> 00:26:24.006
as a solution to burnout.

00:26:24.030 --> 00:26:26.864
AB: I had faith, Adam, I had faith.

00:26:26.888 --> 00:26:28.618
AG: Oh, well, that makes one of us.

00:26:28.642 --> 00:26:30.082
(Both laugh)